  "notes": "The architect of the TDE sound and Kendrick’s principal producer, and the research names his parameter as **adaptation across regimes** rather than a fixed grammar — he works the full 70–150 span. The one constant is the machine lineage ending at an **Akai MPC**, and the MPC feel persists: 2&4 clap and snap with small timing offsets, kicks on 1 and the late \"and-of-3\", 16th hats that thin out under vocals. ⚠ On the live records he **cedes the bass entirely to a played instrument**, which is why the bassline here is independent rather than kick-locked.",
